cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "tanager-cryo: a calibrated cryosphere retrieval for Planet Tanager-1"
message: "If you use this software or its derived data products, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Tang
    given-names: Sean
repository-code: "https://github.com/seantangth/tanager-cryo"
url: "https://seantangth.github.io/tanager-cryo/"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.22163614
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-08-30
abstract: >-
  A physics-based retrieval that inverts Planet Tanager-1 surface reflectance into
  sub-pixel fractions of solid ice/snow, melt pond and dark surface, together with
  effective absorption length (grain size), melt pond depth and light-absorbing
  particle load, with a calibrated per-pixel uncertainty on every quantity.
  Demonstrated on Arctic sea ice in melt at Sirmilik National Park, Nunavut, and
  validated against same-day Sentinel-2C imagery acquired 29 minutes apart.
keywords:
  - hyperspectral
  - imaging spectroscopy
  - cryosphere
  - sea ice
  - melt ponds
  - remote sensing
  - Tanager-1
  - uncertainty quantification
license: Apache-2.0
